Visual Stage fluid renderer

Algorithm source: WebGL Fluid Simulation by Pavel Dobryakov
https://github.com/PavelDoGreat/WebGL-Fluid-Simulation
Original license: https://github.com/PavelDoGreat/WebGL-Fluid-Simulation/blob/master/LICENSE
Retrieved: 2026-10-23

The fluid pass equations in fluid.js are adapted from the MIT source: semi-Lagrangian
advection, bilinear sampling, curl, vorticity confinement, divergence, Jacobi pressure
and gradient subtraction. This offline implementation adds piano-driven emission,
buoyancy and flow fields, WebGL 2 shader translation, lifecycle management, a CPU
advection/pressure fallback, procedural keyboard/note/particle drawing and fifteen
separate material and motion presets. No analytics, network requests, upstream GUI,
dithering bitmap, fonts, video frames, music or third-party logos are included.

Reference names identify visual directions and are not endorsements. Their video
appearance and exact motion fidelity have not been verified from continuous video.
Visual references: https://www.piano-vfx.com/
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=d2qUWg-Rs_w

